; Control code 16: print the subject's name and "is" or "are"
;
; Prints the name of the actor in $B6EA ("you" for the player, "someone" when
; $FF; no article), then returns the word token for "are" when the actor is
; the player and "is" otherwise. The second entry takes the article flag in A
; and the actor in A' (used by #R$7428 for codes 17 and 19).
; .
; The printer calls this handler with IX at the code byte. Return Z when there
; is nothing to print; NZ with a word token in DE and the printer prints it.
;
; A' Actor id (second entry only)
; A Article flag $B703 (second entry only)
; O:DE Word token: $039B "is" or $0065 "are"
; O:F NZ
@label=PrintSubjectIs
c$740C LD A,($B6EA)  ; Subject
 $740F EX AF,AF'     ;
 $7410 XOR A         ;
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$7428.
@label=PrintActorIs
*$7411 LD ($B703),A  ; PhraseMode
 $7414 EX AF,AF'     ;
 $7415 PUSH AF       ;
 $7416 CALL $7488    ;
 $7419 POP AF        ;
 $741A AND A         ;
 $741B LD DE,$039B   ; "is"
 $741E RET NZ        ;
 $741F LD DE,$0065   ; "are"
 $7422 OR $01        ;
 $7424 RET           ;
